# 1. Local Python Environment
# You never upload the virtual environment because it contains thousands of 
# files specific to your operating system. Other developers will install 
# their own using your requirements.txt.
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# 2. Raw Data and Datasets
# Datasets should not be version-controlled. The ml-1m dataset and the 
# zip file are too large and should remain local.
data/
*.dat
*.zip

# 3. Trained Model Weights
# The serialized pickle files (svd_model.pkl, cosine_sim.pkl, etc.) can be 
# quite large. Since you have the train_model.py script, anyone can regenerate 
# these files themselves. 
models/
*.pkl
*.joblib

# 4. Jupyter Notebook Checkpoints
# Jupyter creates hidden auto-save files that clutter the repository.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# 5. Environment Variables
# If you ever add API keys or database passwords later, they go in a .env file.
# This prevents you from accidentally leaking secrets to the public.
.env